%% Nous — evolution of the cognitive (coalition) layer and its dead-ends.
%% See docs/METHODOLOGY.md findings (e) and (f). Each arrow is "what broke -> what was learned".
flowchart TD
    A["Approach 1: connectivity binding<br/>connected components of the co-activated subgraph"]
    A_fail["DEAD END (structural):<br/>a single-seed spread's co-activated subgraph is<br/>connected BY CONSTRUCTION = always ONE coalition"]
    B["Approach 2: flow-magnitude cut<br/>cut the region at weak carried-flow edges"]
    B_part["PARTIAL: now yields more than one coalition,<br/>but keys off DISTANCE-FROM-SEED, not community;<br/>flow is anti-correlated with community near the seed"]
    C["Reframe: multi-source FIELD<br/>many sources = many peaks = basins around peaks"]
    C_ok["Recovers the two communities on the adversarial<br/>bridge graph — but sources were HAND-PLACED<br/>(one per community): the answer was in the input"]
    D["Close the loop: real perception<br/>text = perceive() = input-derived sources = field = coalitions"]
    D_known["KNOWN LIMITATION (asserted in a test):<br/>on clustered real input, basins collapse —<br/>the 'thought' over-swallows; siblings strand as singletons"]
    next["Next step: validate against a MEASURABLE effect<br/>(e.g. semantic priming) whose direction is known<br/>independently of Nous"]

    A --> A_fail -->|"subdivide instead of find one component"| B
    B --> B_part -->|"the fix is upstream of the algorithm"| C
    C --> C_ok -->|"stop hand-placing sources"| D
    D --> D_known -->|"stop choosing inputs that make it pass"| next

    classDef dead fill:#fbeaea,stroke:#c0392b;
    classDef partial fill:#fdf5e6,stroke:#d68910;
    classDef good fill:#eafbea,stroke:#27ae60;
    class A_fail dead;
    class B_part partial;
    class C_ok partial;
    class D_known partial;
    class next good;
